      "excerpts": [
        "South Korea, officially the Republic of Korea (ROK), is a country in East Asia.",
        "It extends over the southern half of the Korean Peninsula and includes the adjacent islands.",
        "It borders North Korea to its north along the Korean Demilitarized Zone, with the Yellow Sea to the west and the Sea of Japan to the east.",
        "It has a population of about 52 million, of which half live in the Seoul metropolitan area, the world's ninth most populous metropolitan area; its other major cities are Busan, Daegu, and Incheon.",
        "The Korean Peninsula was inhabited as early as the Lower Paleolithic period.",
        "Its first kingdom was noted in Chinese records in the early seventh century BC.",
        "From the mid first century BC, various polities consolidated into the rival kingdoms of Goguryeo, Baekje, and Silla.",
        "The latter eventually unified most of the peninsula for the first time in the late seventh century CE, while Balhae succeeded Goguryeo in the north.",
        "The Goryeo dynasty (918–1392) achieved lasting unification and established the basis for Korean identity.",
        "The subsequent Joseon dynasty (1392–1897) generated cultural, economic, and scientific achievements but maintained an isolationist policy from the mid-17th century.",
        "The short-lived Korean Empire (1897–1910) sought modernization and reform but was annexed in 1910 into the Empire of Japan.",
        "Japanese rule ended following Japan's surrender in World War II, after which Korea was divided into two zones: the Soviet-occupied northern zone and the United States-occupied southern zone."
      ]
